Architectures that Highway does not detect (e.g. SPARC) are allowed ("OK to
detect none of the above"), but HWY_ARCH_MAX_BYTES has no case for them.
They only have the EMU128 and SCALAR targets, so use 16 bytes.

Upstream status: to be offered upstream (https://github.com/google/highway)

--- a/hwy/detect_compiler_arch.h	2026-11-27 15:52:21.481767573 +0100
+++ b/hwy/detect_compiler_arch.h	2026-11-27 16:03:59.934772184 +0100
@@ -442,7 +442,8 @@
 #elif HWY_ARCH_PPC || HWY_ARCH_S390X || HWY_ARCH_ARM_V7 || HWY_ARCH_ARM_OLD
 #define HWY_ARCH_MAX_BYTES 16
 #else
-#error "Missing case for HWY_ARCH_*"
+// Other architectures (e.g. SPARC) only have EMU128 and SCALAR.
+#define HWY_ARCH_MAX_BYTES 16
 #endif
 
